{"etape": 12, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T11:26:28.395034Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "I've found the cheapest business class round trip for your dates. Here's the breakdown:\n\n**Cheapest business class round trip (same dates, direct not required):**\n- Outbound 2024-05-26: **HAT023 JFK→SFO** (direct) — business **$364/pax**\n- Return 2024-05-28: **HAT204 SFO→SEA** (business $248) + **HAT100 SEA→JFK** (business $259) = **$507/pax**\n\nTotal per passenger: **$871** · For 3 passengers: **$2,613**\n\n**One important payment limitation:** Per policy, a reservation can use **at most one travel certificate**, up to 3 gift cards, and 1 credit card. So I cannot apply all three of your certificates — only one (I'd use the largest, the $500 certificate, to minimize your card charge).\n\nMaximum payment that can be applied before your card:\n- 1 travel certificate: $500.00\n- 2 gift cards: $198.00 + $129.00 = $327.00\n- **Total applied: $827.00**\n\n**Estimated Mastercard charge: $2,613 − $827 = $1,786.00**\n\nThat $1,786 is **well above** the $567.00 you originally paid for reservation K1NW8N, so per your condition (only book if the Mastercard charge is less than the original amount paid), I would **not** proceed with cancelling or booking.\n\nWould you like to adjust anything — for example, a different cabin, fewer passengers, or not using the card at all?"}, "resultat": "Thank you for the detailed breakdown. I understand the limitations with the certificates and the cost difference.\n\nGiven that the Mastercard charge would be higher than what I originally paid, I will not proceed with cancelling or booking a new flight at this time.\n\nThank you for your help!\n###STOP###", "erreur": null}
